A||||7||Dick McHaffie||New Heater Core?||||1||
Z||000000||Dick McHaffie||03-08-2000||12:30 AM||||Well, I got the 85GT to start reliably and its running really well, but my daughter had been compaining about the windshield fogging.<P>Driving to work this morning I had the same problem.  Heater is blasting HOT air, but most of the windshield stays fogged.<P>Did I mention the sweet smell of coolant?<P>How involved is replacing a heater core?  As you can probably tell from my previous posts, I am by no means an accomplished mechanic.  Should I leave this to the professionals?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||AL||03-08-2000||01:19 AM||||disconnect the hoses,then go inside and take the conveniance center off(where the blue thingy is at)next you will see the black boxs, remove the three bots onthe side, carefully pull the boxs out a little until you see the heater core next remove the upper and lower bolt that holds the core in place,pull the core out and install the new one in and do everything in reverse and you are done, goodluck,AL. ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Gokart||03-08-2000||05:31 AM||||Is there coolant dripping on the passenger side floor? This was the first job I had to do on my GT when I got her a year back and I'm no mechanic either. Piece of cake! The only pain for me was carefully getting the hoses off the old heater core.||||reg||12
Z||000003||BENGAL4||03-08-2000||09:18 AM||||Also take the passenger side speaker out of the dash. This gives you better access to the black box. It's a pain to get that top bolt out if you don't.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||03-08-2000||10:48 AM||||I did mine in about 30 minutes. Hardest part are taking hose off and specially that top bolt of the plastic box inside. Didn't take the speaker off in my case. Just be carefull when removing if the old core still has some coolant inside. Put some rags on the floor just in case.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Patrick||03-09-2000||01:35 AM||||<BR>Your other option is to do it entirely from the spare tire compartment. I don't know if the '85 is different, but on my '87 it was the easiest way to do it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||03-09-2000||07:14 AM||||Sort of along the same line. Where exactly is the A/C condensate drain? When using the A/C for a long trip I get a small drip into the pass. compartment, it's just water not coolant.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dick McHaffie||03-09-2000||12:04 PM||||Well, you guys have given me enough confidence to give this a whirl.<P>The worst thing that could happen is I would have to push the GT a block to my friends garage and pay him to fix it.<P>I would like to get to this weekend, but poor me...I have to go to New Orleans this weekend (I'm in Oregon).  (sigh) I guess the heater will have to wait.<P>Thanks again!  You guys are the best!||||reg||1
